<title>INDIA: Indian money market shut for Independence Day.</title>
<headline>Indian money market shut for Independence Day.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's money market is closed on Friday to celebrate the nation's Independence Day.</p>
<p>Banks reopen on Saturday.</p>
<p>Two-day money ended Thursday at 5.5-6.5 pct and four-day money at 5-6 pct.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91)-22-265 9000</p>
